// The wind that reads: sentences a gust writes across grass or barley, several metres
// tall, gone in a second. The Ledger's voice: present tense, never angry. Keys are
// permanent: add, never rename. These six are taken word for word from the canon
// (the bible's Ledger voice and the prologue) until the owner writes the Vale's own.
{
    "wind.vale.0": "Wind from the north.",
    "wind.vale.1": "Nobody is here.",
    "wind.vale.2": "A crow alights.",
    "wind.vale.3": "Morning, Tithe Hill.",
    "wind.vale.4": "No action is required of you.",
    "wind.vale.5": "You will not recall this notice.",
}
